WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.410 align:middle line:90%


00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.790 align:middle line:90%
Hi, Larry.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:46.450 align:middle line:90%
Hi.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.990 align:middle line:84%
I'm Peggy Nathan, National
Council of Jewish Women.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.560 align:middle line:84%
And I want to thank you so
much for your participating

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.040 align:middle line:84%
in this tremendously
important project.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.180 align:middle line:84%
It, of course, will be
a permanent oral history

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.786 align:middle line:90%
for future generations.

00:01:04.786 --> 00:01:08.770 align:middle line:84%
You, I would like to
introduce as Larry Hersh.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.950 align:middle line:84%
And the first thing we'd
like to do is to tell you--

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:17.273 align:middle line:84%
to have you give me a brief
description of yourself today.

00:01:17.273 --> 00:01:18.260 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.380 align:middle line:84%
Tell me a little
bit about yourself.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.600 align:middle line:84%
Like you said, my
name is Larry Hersh.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.650 align:middle line:84%
I was born in a small
town called Chust--

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:33.340 align:middle line:84%
C-H-U-S-T-- in
Czechoslovakia, 1925.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.330 align:middle line:90%
I'm 59 years old today.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:41.080 align:middle line:90%
I lived there till 19--

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:48.110 align:middle line:90%
till I was taken away in 1942.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:50.690 align:middle line:84%
Well, tell me now, where
do you live now, Larry?

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:55.220 align:middle line:84%
Now, I live in Cleveland
Heights, in the state of Ohio,

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.340 align:middle line:90%
under the address of 2573.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.460 align:middle line:90%
I'm married.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.490 align:middle line:84%
I have three
beautiful daughters.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.530 align:middle line:90%
How lovely.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.650 align:middle line:90%
Are you retired?

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:07.310 align:middle line:90%
Not yet.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:07.810 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.470 align:middle line:84%
But I'm in the
process of retiring.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.012 align:middle line:84%
You're not working
right now, though.

00:02:11.012 --> 00:02:12.680 align:middle line:90%
No, I can't work.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.580 align:middle line:90%
Some of it is part of injuries.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.290 align:middle line:90%
I received.

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.210 align:middle line:84%
And some of it is
part of injuries

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.630 align:middle line:84%
that I brought with
myself from the camps.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:22.130 align:middle line:90%
I understand.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:24.230 align:middle line:90%
And you said you're married.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.430 align:middle line:90%
Does your wife work?

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.438 align:middle line:90%
No, my wife is an American girl.

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:29.480 align:middle line:84%
And fact of the matter is
she's a Cleveland girl.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.560 align:middle line:90%
She was born here.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.090 align:middle line:90%
And her parents were born here.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.260 align:middle line:84%
And what about-- you said
you have three daughters.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.750 align:middle line:84%
They're all born
here in Cleveland.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:39.830 align:middle line:84%
One is in college,
going to be a doctor.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:40.640 align:middle line:90%
How wonderful.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.310 align:middle line:84%
And my second daughter
starts college this year.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:45.710 align:middle line:84%
And my third daughter
is still in high school.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:46.640 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.360 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.787 align:middle line:84%
Now, we're going to really
get into your history--

00:02:50.787 --> 00:02:51.620 align:middle line:90%
To really the point.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.120 align:middle line:90%
--your history, right.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.950 align:middle line:84%
Can you tell me what your
life was like before the war?

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.540 align:middle line:84%
Let's begin with
about 1939 or so.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.710 align:middle line:90%
1939.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:07.220 align:middle line:84%
You were maybe 24 years
old then, is that correct?

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.480 align:middle line:90%
In 1939.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.710 align:middle line:90%
No, in '39, you were--

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:10.220 align:middle line:90%
I'm sorry.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.655 align:middle line:90%
No, in '39 I was--

00:03:11.655 --> 00:03:12.155 align:middle line:90%
You were 14.

00:03:12.155 --> 00:03:12.830 align:middle line:90%
--14 years old.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:13.820 align:middle line:90%
You were born in 1925.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:14.580 align:middle line:90%
'25, yes.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.080 align:middle line:90%
Yes, OK.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.610 align:middle line:90%
I was 14 years old.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.273 align:middle line:90%
I went to school.

00:03:18.273 --> 00:03:19.565 align:middle line:90%
And where were you living then?

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.640 align:middle line:90%
In Chust, Czechoslovakia then.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:22.610 align:middle line:90%
It still was.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:23.510 align:middle line:90%
I see, OK.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.950 align:middle line:90%
This still Czechoslovakia.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.710 align:middle line:84%
Everything was
fine, normal life,

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:35.060 align:middle line:84%
and going to cheder, which
is the Jewish school where

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:40.230 align:middle line:84%
you learn Hebrew and all of the
Jewish rules, laws, and so on.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:40.730 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:44.180 align:middle line:84%
Can you tell me what the
town of Chust was like?

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:44.900 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:50.330 align:middle line:84%
There was a population
of about between--

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.330 align:middle line:84%
there was about
35,000-40,000 population.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:58.550 align:middle line:84%
Between them was about between
8,000 and 10,000 Jewish people.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.050 align:middle line:90%
That was a large proportion.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.610 align:middle line:90%
Yes it was a nice Jewish--

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:03.110 align:middle line:90%
Population.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:04.040 align:middle line:90%
--community.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.990 align:middle line:90%
Yes, a nice Jewish community.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:10.550 align:middle line:84%
There were about a half a
dozen temples, synagogues--

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.060 align:middle line:90%
What big--

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:11.810 align:middle line:90%
--a Hebrew school.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.790 align:middle line:90%
--city were you near?

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.399 align:middle line:90%
Munkács, Kosice.

00:04:16.399 --> 00:04:21.140 align:middle line:84%
It was somewhere-- it's in
the Carpathian Mountains.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:21.890 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:28.190 align:middle line:84%
And it's a section where it
bordered not far with Poland,

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:31.317 align:middle line:84%
from one side, to Romania, from
the other side, and Hungary,

00:04:31.317 --> 00:04:32.150 align:middle line:90%
from the other side.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:32.660 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.970 align:middle line:84%
It was a beautiful,
beautiful country.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.640 align:middle line:84%
Can you tell me about
your family at that time?

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:38.690 align:middle line:90%
We were-- yes.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.280 align:middle line:90%
We were home.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:48.570 align:middle line:84%
I had my grandparents from both
sides of my parents, uncles

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.570 align:middle line:84%
and aunts from both
sides of my parents.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:51.740 align:middle line:90%
But you all lived together?

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:54.200 align:middle line:84%
In the same-- not-- in the
same area, not together.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.430 align:middle line:90%
But not in the same time--

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.480 align:middle line:90%
No, not in the same-- no.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:56.980 align:middle line:90%
--home.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.398 align:middle line:84%
No, not in the same home, but
in the same area, not too far.

00:05:00.398 --> 00:05:01.190 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, I understand.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:07.130 align:middle line:84%
And also, we had some
relatives here in America.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.560 align:middle line:90%
From my mother's side, we had--

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:12.620 align:middle line:84%
she had two brothers
and two sisters here.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:17.330 align:middle line:84%
And my father's side, he had
one brother in California.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:21.350 align:middle line:84%
But I want to know about
your household in Chust.

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:22.440 align:middle line:90%
Am I saying it correctly?

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:22.940 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:23.270 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:23.770 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.190 align:middle line:90%
You lived with your parents?

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:26.390 align:middle line:90%
I lived with my parents.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.093 align:middle line:90%
And later on--

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:29.510 align:middle line:84%
Did you have
brothers and sisters?

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:30.010 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yes.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.670 align:middle line:90%
I had four sisters.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:32.900 align:middle line:90%
And we were five kids.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.580 align:middle line:90%
I was the only boy.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.720 align:middle line:90%
And now, I have only one sister.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.950 align:middle line:90%
Three were young.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.610 align:middle line:84%
And they perished
with my parents.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.220 align:middle line:84%
Now, you saw your
grandparents often, though,

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.088 align:middle line:84%
because they lived in
the same general area.

00:05:47.088 --> 00:05:47.630 align:middle line:90%
Right, right.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.250 align:middle line:84%
How did your family
make a living?

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:51.550 align:middle line:84%
What did your father
do well in those--

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:52.970 align:middle line:90%
just before the war?

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:55.660 align:middle line:84%
My father was a
businessman and happened

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:01.690 align:middle line:84%
to be well-to-do, better than
the most of the Jewish people

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:02.380 align:middle line:90%
around.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:07.480 align:middle line:84%
He was in the wood business,
in other words, like sample.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:08.290 align:middle line:90%
Wood?

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.830 align:middle line:84%
Wood, yeah, buying
forests and cutting them.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:12.490 align:middle line:90%
Certainly.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:16.095 align:middle line:84%
And making-- cutting
into certain lumber.

00:06:16.095 --> 00:06:17.470 align:middle line:84%
We would call them
a lumber yard.

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:19.490 align:middle line:90%
Lumber yard and stuff like that.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.940 align:middle line:90%
And he also had a wine cellar--

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:27.490 align:middle line:84%
wine business, which we bought
the grapes and made the wine.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:33.550 align:middle line:84%
And we were, so to speak--
my father was, so to speak,

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.030 align:middle line:90%
an affluent man in town.

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:36.940 align:middle line:84%
You were-- you would
describe yourself

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.257 align:middle line:90%
as well-to-do or comfortable?

00:06:39.257 --> 00:06:40.840 align:middle line:84%
Well-to-do, right,
comfortable living.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:45.000 align:middle line:84%
And I always as a kid
had everything I wanted.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.750 align:middle line:84%
And in those days,
especially, sports things,

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:52.400 align:middle line:84%
like having my own
football, skiing, skating,

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:53.840 align:middle line:84%
and all of that,
in those days, it

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.360 align:middle line:84%
was a big thing, especially
in the part of the country

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.040 align:middle line:90%
where I was--

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:58.040 align:middle line:90%
Sure, skiing, of course.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:58.820 align:middle line:90%
--and for a kid.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:00.330 align:middle line:90%
And I had all of those things.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:03.470 align:middle line:84%
How would you describe
your family's life?

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:14.930 align:middle line:84%
Well, it is an idealistic life
that you can describe only

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:24.290 align:middle line:84%
in the most seldom-seen
way, let's put it this way.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:26.870 align:middle line:90%
We were all together every meal.

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:31.190 align:middle line:84%
We had-- were together home,
especially the dinners.

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:36.350 align:middle line:84%
And usually, in our time,
the big dinner, the big meal,

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:37.790 align:middle line:90%
was during the dinnertime at--

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:38.710 align:middle line:90%
At noon, you mean?

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:40.070 align:middle line:90%
--at noon, yeah.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.140 align:middle line:90%
And we went to school.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.690 align:middle line:84%
And we used to come home
from school at 1 o'clock.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.580 align:middle line:84%
And by the time 1
o'clock, we used

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:49.003 align:middle line:84%
to sit down and eat,
the entire family.

00:07:49.003 --> 00:07:50.045 align:middle line:90%
Then you went-- how nice.

00:07:50.045 --> 00:07:52.220 align:middle line:84%
And Saturday and the
holidays, there's

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:55.160 align:middle line:84%
nothing to talk about
it, that is unbelievable.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.250 align:middle line:84%
It's just like a
feast, the family

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:00.350 align:middle line:84%
sitting by the table
every Friday night.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:02.480 align:middle line:84%
I used to go with
my father to temple,

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:05.780 align:middle line:84%
and come home, and
have a big meal,

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:12.110 align:middle line:84%
and sing, and go with the
religious, so to speak,

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:16.730 align:middle line:84%
ceremonies that goes with it,
and have the kiddush, the wine.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:19.100 align:middle line:84%
And for Saturday
morning, we used

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:24.590 align:middle line:84%
to all get dressed up fancy,
was the holiday clothes,

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:27.620 align:middle line:84%
so to speak, and go to
Temple again in the morning

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.860 align:middle line:90%
and come home, have a big meal.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.840 align:middle line:84%
Religion played a big
part in your life.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.919 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:08:33.919 --> 00:08:43.669 align:middle line:84%
Well, it-- yes, it was not
in the sense of fanaticism

00:08:43.669 --> 00:08:52.190 align:middle line:84%
of the religion, but it was
with a sensible religious way.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:56.000 align:middle line:84%
How about Zionism or other
political organizations?

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.060 align:middle line:84%
Was your family interested
or involved in that?

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:01.400 align:middle line:84%
Can you remember
back in those years?

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.780 align:middle line:90%
Oh, I do remember well.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.820 align:middle line:90%
I was very much involved.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:11.390 align:middle line:84%
And my father, he was involved
just by being, so to speak,

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:17.090 align:middle line:84%
supporting one organization or
the other in terms of money.

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:20.630 align:middle line:84%
He did not participate in
too many of those meetings

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:21.440 align:middle line:90%
and all of that.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.410 align:middle line:84%
But therefore, I already
made up for him too.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.090 align:middle line:84%
You were a member
of a Zionist group?

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.160 align:middle line:84%
I was a member of the
Zionist organization.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.260 align:middle line:84%
I was the leader of a
Zionist organization,

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.750 align:middle line:90%
the whole area of Betar.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.070 align:middle line:90%
This was in your teen years?

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:35.660 align:middle line:90%
Right, of Betar.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:38.090 align:middle line:84%
And as I grew older,
as we come to it,

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.260 align:middle line:84%
we will come to it a
little bit later on,

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.980 align:middle line:84%
you will see the
whole operations

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:46.170 align:middle line:84%
and so forth that I was
involved my entire life.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:49.260 align:middle line:84%
Did socialism or any other
political organizations

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:51.240 align:middle line:90%
play a part in your family life?

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:54.730 align:middle line:84%
Socialism not-- well,
we knew about it.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:55.740 align:middle line:90%
We talked about it.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:00.360 align:middle line:90%
But my father could not--

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.210 align:middle line:84%
he was considered to be a
bourgeois because the fact

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.910 align:middle line:84%
that he was rich and
he was a well-to-do.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:09.360 align:middle line:84%
So he could not be
a communist already.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:12.840 align:middle line:84%
Socialism, that was-- we knew
what's going on in Russia.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:16.620 align:middle line:84%
And we know-- we knew that
the little success they have

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:17.590 align:middle line:90%
with communism.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.580 align:middle line:84%
We know that in the '30s that
the hunger has been going on

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.340 align:middle line:90%
in Russia and all of that.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:27.638 align:middle line:84%
It-- we knew what's going
on in Germany with Hitler.

00:10:27.638 --> 00:10:30.180 align:middle line:84%
And we knew what was going on
in the world, far as this goes,

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:34.288 align:middle line:84%
because of radio and as far as
communication was and wasn't.

00:10:34.288 --> 00:10:35.580 align:middle line:90%
You were aware of world things.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.410 align:middle line:84%
We were aware worldwide
what's going on.

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:40.890 align:middle line:84%
We knew-- for
example, we even know

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:44.170 align:middle line:84%
what's going on in
America, the Depression.

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:47.780 align:middle line:84%
And we had a little bit of a
firsthand knowledge of that.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:50.300 align:middle line:84%
In 1933, one of
my uncles-- like I

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:53.030 align:middle line:84%
said, do you remember, I
said, I have a-- my father

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:54.080 align:middle line:90%
had a brother.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.800 align:middle line:84%
His brother came to visit,
came home to Europe.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:58.410 align:middle line:90%
From America?

00:10:58.410 --> 00:10:58.910 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:01.220 align:middle line:84%
And he came home from
America for a visit.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:04.430 align:middle line:90%
And one day, he got a telegram.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.800 align:middle line:90%
We-- I was a kid.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:08.120 align:middle line:90%
I don't remember what it was.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:11.930 align:middle line:84%
But a few days afterwards,
he packed and he left.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:16.610 align:middle line:84%
Later on, I found out
that he had some--

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:17.633 align:middle line:90%
he was in business.

00:11:17.633 --> 00:11:19.550 align:middle line:84%
And he had some kind of
business difficulties.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:21.950 align:middle line:84%
And he-- they
needed his presence

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.360 align:middle line:90%
because of the circumstances.

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.710 align:middle line:90%
And he left.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:27.620 align:middle line:84%
And his mother cried
bitterly that he left.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:32.660 align:middle line:84%
And that was the end, probably,
that he ever saw his family.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:35.810 align:middle line:84%
What was the main language
spoken in your home?

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:38.870 align:middle line:84%
In my home-- in the house, the
main language that was spoken

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:40.850 align:middle line:90%
is Yiddish.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:44.130 align:middle line:84%
We also, all the kids
and the entire family,

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:47.850 align:middle line:84%
everybody in the family, from
my uncles and grandparents, all

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.590 align:middle line:90%
the way, we had--

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:52.470 align:middle line:84%
they had at least
three different--

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.900 align:middle line:90%
know three different languages.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:12:00.240 align:middle line:84%
I, in school, learned already
a little bit of German.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.400 align:middle line:84%
And I knew a little
bit of Hebrew

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.020 align:middle line:84%
already-- not in
the sense-- there

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:07.020 align:middle line:84%
was one thing in the prayers,
but the other in the Hebrew.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.500 align:middle line:90%
So it was a different.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:09.210 align:middle line:90%
So I knew some.

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.293 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, the spoken language.

00:12:10.293 --> 00:12:15.150 align:middle line:84%
We spoke Hungarian, Czech,
and the local, so to speak,

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:15.960 align:middle line:90%
Russian.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.940 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.980 align:middle line:84%
Were there many
books in your home?

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.895 align:middle line:84%
Were you-- was your
family interested in that?

00:12:22.895 --> 00:12:24.550 align:middle line:90%
Yes, we had books.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.420 align:middle line:84%
But there was no
library in town.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:29.890 align:middle line:84%
But there was a different
way of doing things.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.370 align:middle line:84%
For example, if a
new book came out,

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:35.130 align:middle line:84%
I remember reading
Gone with the Wind

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:37.110 align:middle line:90%
in four different languages.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.130 align:middle line:90%
Can you imagine?

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:40.950 align:middle line:90%


00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:47.870 align:middle line:84%
Thomas-- what was his name, I
believe, the president's man--

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.840 align:middle line:90%


00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:54.510 align:middle line:84%
and Steinbeck, I
read those books

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:58.190 align:middle line:84%
in three or four
different languages.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.750 align:middle line:84%
Well, where did you
get these books?

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:00.980 align:middle line:90%
The style was like this.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.930 align:middle line:90%
For example, I had friends.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.910 align:middle line:84%
And we knew there
is a new book out.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:06.890 align:middle line:90%
So I bought one book.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.220 align:middle line:90%
He bought a different one.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.250 align:middle line:84%
So you would-- you had
your own lending library.

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:12.050 align:middle line:84%
Then we switched around
between ourselves,

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:15.440 align:middle line:84%
and went from hand to
hand, and so on, and so on.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.132 align:middle line:84%
Was there a theater or a
concert hall in the town?

00:13:18.132 --> 00:13:18.965 align:middle line:90%
Yes, there was-- no.

00:13:18.965 --> 00:13:20.480 align:middle line:90%
A museum of any kind?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.860 align:middle line:84%
No, no museum, nothing
of this nature.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.238 align:middle line:90%
But a concert-- we listened--

00:13:26.238 --> 00:13:27.655 align:middle line:84%
we didn't pay too
much attention--

00:13:27.655 --> 00:13:28.010 align:middle line:90%
You weren't that.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:28.790 align:middle line:90%
--to the concert.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.240 align:middle line:90%
But we had a movie house.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.520 align:middle line:84%
And fact of the matter is
we had two movie houses.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.970 align:middle line:84%
And we used to go almost
every night to a movie.

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:36.950 align:middle line:90%
That was the main entertainment.

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:37.880 align:middle line:90%
Were the movies.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:38.630 align:middle line:90%
Movies.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:42.350 align:middle line:84%
And then close to the Jewish
holidays, like a Purim,

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:45.810 align:middle line:84%
or in the wintertime,
usually, used to come a--

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:50.850 align:middle line:84%
we used to call them a
troupe, a Jewish group playing

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:51.840 align:middle line:90%
Jewish theater.

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.420 align:middle line:84%
And they stayed for
a week or two weeks.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:55.305 align:middle line:90%
And would entertain.

00:13:55.305 --> 00:13:56.550 align:middle line:84%
Right, and then they
used to keep going.

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:57.510 align:middle line:90%
Live entertainment.

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:58.010 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:13:58.010 --> 00:14:00.840 align:middle line:84%
And then used to
go to the next one.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.000 align:middle line:90%
Did your family go on vacations?

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.545 align:middle line:90%
Yes, we used to have--

00:14:04.545 --> 00:14:07.560 align:middle line:90%


00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.690 align:middle line:84%
ours was already
considered a big town.

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:14.370 align:middle line:84%
Like I said, we had 35-40, maybe
a few more thousand people.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.940 align:middle line:84%
It was considered to
be already a nice town.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.130 align:middle line:84%
So we used to go
to the countryside

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:25.740 align:middle line:84%
almost every summer, around
July, August, something

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.990 align:middle line:90%
like that, for a month.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:33.600 align:middle line:84%
And to understand how the
Carpathian Mountains is one

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.490 align:middle line:90%
of the most beautiful part of--

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:38.820 align:middle line:84%
in any country, which you
could have there mushrooms

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:41.940 align:middle line:84%
and all kind of berries,
and swimming, and fishing,

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:45.780 align:middle line:84%
and mineral waters, and
mineral baths to be taken.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.820 align:middle line:90%
It was just beautiful.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:49.320 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.230 align:middle line:84%
Now, let's talk about
you, personally.

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:55.470 align:middle line:84%
How do you remember
yourself in those days?

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:56.372 align:middle line:90%
Myself, I remember--

00:14:56.372 --> 00:14:57.330 align:middle line:90%
What did you look like?

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:57.830 align:middle line:90%
I looked--

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.130 align:middle line:90%
Handsome?

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:03.930 align:middle line:84%
I was a young boy who
loved swimming, loved

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:08.730 align:middle line:84%
playing football, who loved
running, bicycling, loved

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:13.550 align:middle line:84%
to go steal apples from the
neighbor, steal pears and--

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.760 align:middle line:90%
An all-around boy.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.020 align:middle line:90%
All-around boy.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:19.410 align:middle line:84%
Did you have any
special interests other

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:20.580 align:middle line:90%
than the sports?

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.230 align:middle line:84%
You mentioned, you
love the sports.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:25.440 align:middle line:84%
Yes, I played soccer
almost every team--

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:26.730 align:middle line:90%
we had-- every day.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.170 align:middle line:90%
And we had our own team.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:32.460 align:middle line:84%
And we used to play team against
team, and town against town,

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.350 align:middle line:90%
and so on.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:37.500 align:middle line:90%
It was just everything right.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:41.400 align:middle line:84%
You have beautiful
memories of your childhood.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:44.120 align:middle line:84%
Tell you the truth,
that keep me going.

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:45.340 align:middle line:90%
It was everything beautiful.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:49.570 align:middle line:84%
This is till the-- my age
of 20 when I was still.

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:51.700 align:middle line:84%
I left the age of
17, I should say,

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:55.650 align:middle line:84%
because after this,
it's camp and all that.

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:56.860 align:middle line:90%
It was nothing.

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:59.180 align:middle line:84%
I had everything
my heart desired.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:15:59.680 align:middle line:90%
How nice.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.730 align:middle line:90%
I did everything I wanted.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:06.640 align:middle line:84%
And it's like somebody put
all together a package for me

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:08.620 align:middle line:84%
till the age of
17 that everything

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:10.195 align:middle line:90%
will be put together.

00:16:10.195 --> 00:16:14.230 align:middle line:84%
Tell me, what kind of
schools did you attend?

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:15.670 align:middle line:90%
Like I said, I attend cheder.

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:18.430 align:middle line:90%
Then I attended Czech school.

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:19.260 align:middle line:90%
I went to Czech--

00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:21.250 align:middle line:84%
But the cheder is just
the religious school?

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:21.550 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:22.175 align:middle line:90%
Regular, right.

00:16:22.175 --> 00:16:24.430 align:middle line:84%
I went to Czech
elementary school.

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.530 align:middle line:90%
And then I went-- started--

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:30.370 align:middle line:84%
by the time change came, I
started to go to Hungarian.

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:35.950 align:middle line:84%
And I went to high school,
which was called gymnasium

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:38.108 align:middle line:90%
instead of high school.

00:16:38.108 --> 00:16:38.650 align:middle line:90%
I understand.

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:43.820 align:middle line:84%
And till around
the fourth class,

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:46.250 align:middle line:84%
then I had to quit
because Jews were not

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.343 align:middle line:90%
permitted to go to school.

00:16:47.343 --> 00:16:49.010 align:middle line:84%
That was-- and so how
many years had you

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:50.720 align:middle line:84%
gone to school
altogether in Europe?

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.250 align:middle line:90%
Let's see, I had to--

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:58.820 align:middle line:84%
I started out-- my
first year was in 1931.

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:00.260 align:middle line:90%
And I went--

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:03.650 align:middle line:84%
I had altogether about
nine years of schooling.

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:07.190 align:middle line:84%
Did you have any
non-Jewish friends?

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:11.210 align:middle line:84%
Oh, yes, I had many
non-Jewish friends.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:15.670 align:middle line:84%
And I also had many
non-Jewish enemies,

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:20.569 align:middle line:84%
with which I had to conduct
it very often too many fights.

00:17:20.569 --> 00:17:23.180 align:middle line:84%
What do you remember
about antisemitism

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:26.030 align:middle line:84%
in those days of your--
your school days?

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:31.700 align:middle line:84%
In my school days, it had
a peculiar sense to it.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:34.940 align:middle line:90%
It was a different--

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:38.270 align:middle line:84%
it wasn't in the
sense as antisemitism

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:40.160 align:middle line:90%
as it's known today.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:46.490 align:middle line:84%
It was more of a, so to
speak, religious bigotry.

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:49.610 align:middle line:84%
In the sense, for an
example, we didn't know--

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:52.190 align:middle line:84%
we could see and
feel when, let's say,

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:57.380 align:middle line:84%
my Gentile friends went
to church Sunday and what

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:02.920 align:middle line:84%
the preacher-- what his sermon
was and if it was anti-Jewish

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.700 align:middle line:90%
or--

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:08.300 align:middle line:84%
in the way they acted, in
other words, in the way--

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:11.150 align:middle line:84%
they used to say that good
morning or that good day

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.720 align:middle line:84%
or how we used to play football
in the afternoon with the kids.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:18.570 align:middle line:84%
Or there was times,
for an example,

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.780 align:middle line:84%
that they will do
anything for you,

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:24.170 align:middle line:84%
that you would know any--
no boundaries, no difference

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:25.070 align:middle line:90%
whatsoever.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:29.150 align:middle line:84%
Then another time,
was Jesus killer,

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:34.350 align:middle line:84%
that kind of rotten Jew,
and all that kind of thing.

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:38.900 align:middle line:84%
But I would say, we could
live together like this,

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:41.830 align:middle line:84%
if it had stayed like this,
for another 1,000 years,

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.180 align:middle line:90%
and nothing would have happened.

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:46.460 align:middle line:84%
And everything would
have been going smoothly.

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:47.860 align:middle line:90%
And then it gets tough.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:50.500 align:middle line:84%
You have a fight
there between kids.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:51.320 align:middle line:90%
Well, childhood.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:51.820 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:54.340 align:middle line:84%
Young childhood,
yeah, pranks, and then

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.950 align:middle line:84%
Jews playing against
the Gentiles,

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:59.300 align:middle line:90%
and that kind of stuff.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:04.030 align:middle line:84%
But it had no serious meaning
of any kind of consequence.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.740 align:middle line:90%
Well OK.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:08.110 align:middle line:90%
Now, we'll get on to--

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:11.350 align:middle line:84%
all right, these
were your teen years.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:16.300 align:middle line:84%
What do you remember about
the beginning of World War II?

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:16.900 align:middle line:90%
World War II--

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:20.620 align:middle line:84%
When were you first aware
that there was a war?

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:23.950 align:middle line:84%
My beginning of World
War two is started out

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:29.260 align:middle line:84%
in 1938, when Hitler
started in the Sudeten.

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:34.210 align:middle line:84%
We already began to feel
the punch in Czechoslovakia.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:37.840 align:middle line:84%
The Germans and
the Sudetengebiet,

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:44.160 align:middle line:84%
which was called, starting to
make trouble in Czechoslovakia,

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.240 align:middle line:84%
then creating all kind of
confrontations and all of that.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:51.290 align:middle line:84%
What made you aware that
there were things going on?

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:54.350 align:middle line:84%
Well, we knew what's going
on in the world scene.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:57.860 align:middle line:84%
We know that Germany
occupied Austria.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:03.230 align:middle line:84%
And we knew what's going on with
the Jewish people and Hitler's

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:04.370 align:middle line:90%
Germany.

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:07.040 align:middle line:84%
And we knew what's going on
with the Jewish in Vienna

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:10.020 align:middle line:84%
after he moved in in
Austria and so on.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:14.840 align:middle line:84%
And we knew that nothing
good will come out of it.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:15.500 align:middle line:90%
Excuse me.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:16.100 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:23.040 align:middle line:84%
But nobody dreamed that it
will go in such a fast pace

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:27.710 align:middle line:84%
in the way it went and it will
have such a devastating results

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:29.120 align:middle line:90%
as it had.

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:33.050 align:middle line:84%
Were there changes in the way
that non-Jews acted toward you

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:34.460 align:middle line:90%
and your family then?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:37.160 align:middle line:84%
At that point in
time, we still--

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:42.450 align:middle line:84%
it's-- they are occupying
only the Sudeten part.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:45.313 align:middle line:90%
We are still Czechoslovakia.

00:20:45.313 --> 00:20:49.050 align:middle line:90%
It's-- everybody is restless.

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:51.318 align:middle line:84%
And nobody knows
in what direction.

00:20:51.318 --> 00:20:52.860 align:middle line:84%
The fact of-- the
truth of the matter

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:57.630 align:middle line:84%
is that even some of the
Gentiles were afraid.

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:03.510 align:middle line:84%
Because they did not know
what is awaiting, who is what.

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:06.370 align:middle line:84%
And then the major
change came, I remember,

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:12.023 align:middle line:90%
and it was in September--

00:21:12.023 --> 00:21:12.565 align:middle line:90%
Of what year?

00:21:12.565 --> 00:21:16.780 align:middle line:90%
--of the month of 1939.

00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:24.160 align:middle line:84%
No, no that was in
1939 in early spring.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:26.117 align:middle line:90%
Then it came the change--

00:21:26.117 --> 00:21:26.950 align:middle line:90%
What kind of change?

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:28.300 align:middle line:90%
--of a big scale.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.540 align:middle line:90%
Czechoslovakia fall apart.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:33.100 align:middle line:90%
You mean the government?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:33.800 align:middle line:90%
Completely.

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.640 align:middle line:84%
In other words, Czechoslovakia
as a country fall apart.

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:39.760 align:middle line:90%


00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:44.290 align:middle line:84%
The Germans moved in to
Prague, occupied the entire top

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:45.500 align:middle line:90%
of Czechoslovakia.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:51.100 align:middle line:90%
Poland took a part by Silesia.

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:54.370 align:middle line:84%
The Hungarians took
the rest of it.

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:58.660 align:middle line:84%
And we, in the
Carpathian Mountains,

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:00.400 align:middle line:90%
we became part of Hungary.

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:01.790 align:middle line:90%
We were occupied by Hungary.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:02.290 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:05.920 align:middle line:84%
And then the change
was right away.

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:07.900 align:middle line:84%
Well, what changes
did your family

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:10.130 align:middle line:90%
have to make because of that?

00:22:10.130 --> 00:22:14.300 align:middle line:84%
First of all that Czech
schools was closed right away.

00:22:14.300 --> 00:22:16.700 align:middle line:90%
There was no school.

00:22:16.700 --> 00:22:19.760 align:middle line:84%
Everything was changed
from the Czech language

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:22.858 align:middle line:90%
to the Hungarian language.

00:22:22.858 --> 00:22:23.900 align:middle line:90%
Well, you were fortunate.

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:25.070 align:middle line:90%
You knew the language.

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:26.090 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:22:26.090 --> 00:22:27.800 align:middle line:90%
They didn't bother us.

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:35.090 align:middle line:84%
But there were some people who
remembered the Hungarians prior

00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:36.080 align:middle line:90%
to Czechoslovakia.

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:38.990 align:middle line:84%
You got to remember
that Czechoslovakia

00:22:38.990 --> 00:22:43.400 align:middle line:84%
came into existence after the
World War I. And prior to that,

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:47.480 align:middle line:84%
it was under the
Hungarian Austrian Empire.

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:50.720 align:middle line:84%
So some people remember
the old Tsar and--

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:55.760 align:middle line:84%
I mean the old king, and Franz
Joseph, and all of that era--

00:22:55.760 --> 00:22:57.050 align:middle line:90%
my grandfather.

00:22:57.050 --> 00:23:00.410 align:middle line:84%
And he had a certain, so to
speak, feeling towards that.

00:23:00.410 --> 00:23:02.480 align:middle line:84%
It didn't feel terrible
that this was happening?

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:03.260 align:middle line:90%
No.

00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:04.650 align:middle line:90%
It's just change.

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:05.330 align:middle line:90%
Change, right.

00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:08.570 align:middle line:84%
And they felt that everything
will in time improve.

00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:13.460 align:middle line:84%
And it's just one of
those historical facts.

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:15.497 align:middle line:84%
The Czechoslovakia
disappeared as a country,

00:23:15.497 --> 00:23:16.330 align:middle line:90%
as a Czechoslovakia.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:17.080 align:middle line:90%
And that was that.

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:20.710 align:middle line:84%
But did it-- did that in
itself affect your family?

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:22.930 align:middle line:84%
The family as a
whole, it did not

00:23:22.930 --> 00:23:25.280 align:middle line:84%
affect because we
were still all home.

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:26.650 align:middle line:90%
We were all together.

00:23:26.650 --> 00:23:28.720 align:middle line:90%
And each one, business as usual.

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:32.410 align:middle line:84%
The fact of the matter
is after a little while,

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:37.330 align:middle line:84%
my father did command his
business with the Hungarians

00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:39.895 align:middle line:90%
because they started--

00:23:39.895 --> 00:23:43.390 align:middle line:84%
and a year or two later down,
until we were taken away

00:23:43.390 --> 00:23:47.600 align:middle line:84%
from home in 1940 and '41,
we have a tremendous business

00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:48.100 align:middle line:90%
with them.

00:23:48.100 --> 00:23:50.590 align:middle line:84%
Because they bought all
kinds of materials--

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:54.550 align:middle line:84%
raw materials, wood,
fruits, wines, everything.

00:23:54.550 --> 00:23:57.868 align:middle line:84%
And they were exporting it to
Germany, to the German Army.

00:23:57.868 --> 00:23:58.660 align:middle line:90%
They were already--

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:00.067 align:middle line:90%
And excellent business.

00:24:00.067 --> 00:24:01.150 align:middle line:90%
So this business was good.

00:24:01.150 --> 00:24:01.780 align:middle line:90%
Of course.

00:24:01.780 --> 00:24:03.250 align:middle line:90%
Yes, it was excellent business.

00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:05.137 align:middle line:84%
Were you worried
about the future?

00:24:05.137 --> 00:24:06.970 align:middle line:84%
Or you thought things
were going to be good?

00:24:06.970 --> 00:24:13.480 align:middle line:84%
As time progressed, and as
we existed, in other words,

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:16.250 align:middle line:90%
in our existence, we felt good.

00:24:16.250 --> 00:24:18.310 align:middle line:90%
We had everything we needed.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:19.930 align:middle line:90%
There was nothing missing.

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:24.190 align:middle line:84%
Nobody bothered us
as on a serious way.

00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:26.320 align:middle line:84%
We didn't realize
that we have been

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:28.330 align:middle line:90%
living in a fool's paradise.

00:24:28.330 --> 00:24:32.110 align:middle line:84%
Because the world
burning around us.

00:24:32.110 --> 00:24:34.180 align:middle line:84%
And you know how
human nature is.

00:24:34.180 --> 00:24:34.690 align:middle line:90%
Of course.

00:24:34.690 --> 00:24:39.130 align:middle line:84%
So we-- if I have
my loaf of bread,

00:24:39.130 --> 00:24:43.510 align:middle line:84%
that several hundred
kilometers away from here,

00:24:43.510 --> 00:24:45.550 align:middle line:84%
something else is going
on, it didn't bother.

00:24:45.550 --> 00:24:48.520 align:middle line:84%
And it was something what's
far away and is happening.

00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:51.500 align:middle line:84%
And that's exactly the
way it happened with us.

00:24:51.500 --> 00:24:52.000 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:55.420 align:middle line:84%
Then eventually, the
Nazis entered your town?

00:24:55.420 --> 00:24:57.200 align:middle line:90%
No, not yet.

00:24:57.200 --> 00:25:05.590 align:middle line:84%
Then in 1942-- '41,
slowly, laws starting

00:25:05.590 --> 00:25:07.330 align:middle line:90%
to come out against the Jews.

00:25:07.330 --> 00:25:08.590 align:middle line:90%
Right, the Nuremberg laws.

00:25:08.590 --> 00:25:12.230 align:middle line:84%
Jews cannot-- these-- that-- the
Nuremberg laws were out already

00:25:12.230 --> 00:25:13.340 align:middle line:90%
quite a while.

00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:15.635 align:middle line:84%
But they starting to
take effect in Hungary.

00:25:15.635 --> 00:25:16.310 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:25:16.310 --> 00:25:18.135 align:middle line:90%
Jews were beaten on the streets.

00:25:18.135 --> 00:25:21.500 align:middle line:84%
Well, who-- were there
Nazis there doing this?

00:25:21.500 --> 00:25:22.070 align:middle line:90%
They are.

00:25:22.070 --> 00:25:24.830 align:middle line:84%
In the meantime, a Nazi
Party was formed already.

00:25:24.830 --> 00:25:28.520 align:middle line:84%
And they started to make
all kinds of propaganda.

00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:35.270 align:middle line:84%
And in my area, the major
non-Jewish population,

00:25:35.270 --> 00:25:36.830 align:middle line:90%
they were not involved.

00:25:36.830 --> 00:25:39.560 align:middle line:84%
They were always only the
few who were involved.

00:25:39.560 --> 00:25:42.890 align:middle line:84%
And you always will
find a few in everywhere

00:25:42.890 --> 00:25:46.060 align:middle line:84%
that they are willing to sell
their soul for-- you know.

00:25:46.060 --> 00:25:47.060 align:middle line:90%
Right, right.

00:25:47.060 --> 00:25:49.670 align:middle line:90%
And they gave in.

00:25:49.670 --> 00:25:51.110 align:middle line:90%
Laws came out.

00:25:51.110 --> 00:25:52.280 align:middle line:90%
You couldn't go here.

00:25:52.280 --> 00:25:54.020 align:middle line:90%
You couldn't go there.

00:25:54.020 --> 00:25:56.810 align:middle line:84%
And the soldier going
around on a rampage,

00:25:56.810 --> 00:26:01.640 align:middle line:84%
beating people with a
beard, and beating here.

00:26:01.640 --> 00:26:04.790 align:middle line:84%
They found out where a Jewish
family lives, come at night,

00:26:04.790 --> 00:26:08.210 align:middle line:84%
and break the
windows, and scream,

00:26:08.210 --> 00:26:11.640 align:middle line:90%
holler, make all kind of--

00:26:11.640 --> 00:26:15.580 align:middle line:84%
behaving just like
a mob behaves.

00:26:15.580 --> 00:26:18.400 align:middle line:84%
And we had to learn
how to contend with it.

00:26:18.400 --> 00:26:19.330 align:middle line:90%
And we did.

00:26:19.330 --> 00:26:24.200 align:middle line:84%
But your family made their
living in the same way.

00:26:24.200 --> 00:26:26.350 align:middle line:84%
Well, the living
started to go down.

00:26:26.350 --> 00:26:29.090 align:middle line:84%
Business started to
be badly already.

00:26:29.090 --> 00:26:33.100 align:middle line:84%
And in fact, then the business
was taken away and given

00:26:33.100 --> 00:26:35.470 align:middle line:90%
to a non-Jew, who--

00:26:35.470 --> 00:26:38.810 align:middle line:84%
some of the Hungarians
brought in from deep Hungary,

00:26:38.810 --> 00:26:40.960 align:middle line:84%
which we didn't even know
who he is and took away

00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:42.310 align:middle line:90%
our businesses.

00:26:42.310 --> 00:26:44.500 align:middle line:84%
The only thing what
was left is our house

00:26:44.500 --> 00:26:45.970 align:middle line:90%
and that we could stay there.

00:26:45.970 --> 00:26:48.910 align:middle line:84%
So then how long
did you stay there?

00:26:48.910 --> 00:26:50.590 align:middle line:84%
Your family was
moved eventually.

00:26:50.590 --> 00:26:52.440 align:middle line:84%
Eventually, yes, we
were all moved later on.

00:26:52.440 --> 00:26:52.540 align:middle line:90%
We came to the ghettos.

00:26:52.540 --> 00:26:52.960 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:26:52.960 --> 00:26:54.252 align:middle line:90%
But so things were getting bad.

00:26:54.252 --> 00:26:55.340 align:middle line:90%
The business was taken.

00:26:55.340 --> 00:26:55.840 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:26:55.840 --> 00:26:56.960 align:middle line:90%
The business was taken.

00:26:56.960 --> 00:26:58.760 align:middle line:84%
And everything starting
to go downhill.

00:26:58.760 --> 00:26:59.260 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:26:59.260 --> 00:27:04.480 align:middle line:84%
Antisemitism became
more a way of life

00:27:04.480 --> 00:27:07.960 align:middle line:84%
with the local population,
with the local people.

00:27:07.960 --> 00:27:11.300 align:middle line:84%
The young generation,
the young people, friends

00:27:11.300 --> 00:27:15.210 align:middle line:84%
with whom I used to play soccer
yesterday didn't know me today.

00:27:15.210 --> 00:27:19.550 align:middle line:84%
And it was only one,
maybe two who felt sorry.

00:27:19.550 --> 00:27:22.860 align:middle line:84%
But they were afraid
to do anything.

00:27:22.860 --> 00:27:28.250 align:middle line:84%
And that was going on not only
in the younger generation,

00:27:28.250 --> 00:27:30.710 align:middle line:84%
but also, spilled over
to the older ones.

00:27:30.710 --> 00:27:38.160 align:middle line:84%
In other words, for example,
my father knew other fathers.

00:27:38.160 --> 00:27:40.160 align:middle line:90%
And he grew up there together.

00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:42.290 align:middle line:90%
Yet--

00:27:42.290 --> 00:27:43.980 align:middle line:84%
They no longer
spoke to each other.

00:27:43.980 --> 00:27:46.500 align:middle line:84%
They did, but it
didn't mean anything.

00:27:46.500 --> 00:27:48.050 align:middle line:90%
They-- don't bother me.

00:27:48.050 --> 00:27:49.110 align:middle line:90%
I can't do it.

00:27:49.110 --> 00:27:49.610 align:middle line:90%
It was--

00:27:49.610 --> 00:27:49.890 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:27:49.890 --> 00:27:50.930 align:middle line:90%
Nobody took your part.

00:27:50.930 --> 00:27:52.230 align:middle line:90%
Nobody helped you.

00:27:52.230 --> 00:27:52.730 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:27:52.730 --> 00:27:56.900 align:middle line:84%
Nobody was-- and in
fact, my grandparents

00:27:56.900 --> 00:28:01.280 align:middle line:84%
lived in a village not far from
our hometown, from our town,

00:28:01.280 --> 00:28:05.960 align:middle line:84%
from Chust, about 50 or
60 kilometers from there.

00:28:05.960 --> 00:28:11.630 align:middle line:84%
And that small village,
there were maybe

00:28:11.630 --> 00:28:14.270 align:middle line:90%
30 or 40 Jewish families.

00:28:14.270 --> 00:28:18.257 align:middle line:84%
And there was about
500 or more non-Jews.

00:28:18.257 --> 00:28:19.840 align:middle line:84%
They started-- and
they grew up there.

00:28:19.840 --> 00:28:21.970 align:middle line:84%
They lived all their
life in that village.

00:28:21.970 --> 00:28:24.700 align:middle line:84%
Yet they starting already
to feel the pinch.

00:28:24.700 --> 00:28:27.760 align:middle line:90%
They wouldn't sell them wood.

00:28:27.760 --> 00:28:29.710 align:middle line:84%
And they wouldn't
sell them products.

00:28:29.710 --> 00:28:31.412 align:middle line:90%
They would not do this.

00:28:31.412 --> 00:28:33.370 align:middle line:84%
And the usual thing, they
used to be everything

00:28:33.370 --> 00:28:35.620 align:middle line:90%
without any change.

00:28:35.620 --> 00:28:36.550 align:middle line:90%
Nobody was around.

00:28:36.550 --> 00:28:37.050 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:28:37.050 --> 00:28:40.720 align:middle line:84%
Looking back, and
you knew-- you saw

00:28:40.720 --> 00:28:44.830 align:middle line:84%
what was happening-- do
you recall any plans, then,

00:28:44.830 --> 00:28:49.600 align:middle line:84%
that your family made to
deal with this situation?

00:28:49.600 --> 00:28:51.700 align:middle line:84%
Or did they feel that
they were helpless?

00:28:51.700 --> 00:28:54.430 align:middle line:84%
They was-- let me
give you a sense

00:28:54.430 --> 00:28:57.640 align:middle line:84%
to understanding from the
Jewish point of view what

00:28:57.640 --> 00:28:58.750 align:middle line:90%
has been going on.

00:28:58.750 --> 00:29:01.360 align:middle line:84%
Well, I want to know,
though, about you, yourself,

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:02.410 align:middle line:90%
and your family.

00:29:02.410 --> 00:29:04.900 align:middle line:84%
Yeah, it was me and my-- it
was-- involves me my family.

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:05.400 align:middle line:90%
OK, fine.

00:29:05.400 --> 00:29:08.800 align:middle line:84%
But in the way things been
going with me and my family

00:29:08.800 --> 00:29:12.678 align:middle line:84%
will reflect on the
entire concept of--

00:29:12.678 --> 00:29:13.970 align:middle line:90%
Right, and I understand, right.

00:29:13.970 --> 00:29:16.530 align:middle line:84%
--existing at that
period of time.

00:29:16.530 --> 00:29:19.160 align:middle line:90%
I was a very good student.

00:29:19.160 --> 00:29:22.850 align:middle line:84%
And in 1938, in
Czechoslovakia, was

00:29:22.850 --> 00:29:30.080 align:middle line:84%
a school in Prague for
special talented youngsters.

00:29:30.080 --> 00:29:33.350 align:middle line:84%
I had to go through, I
remember, a special test.

00:29:33.350 --> 00:29:37.090 align:middle line:84%
And I came out
with flying colors.

00:29:37.090 --> 00:29:40.760 align:middle line:84%
They sent me a
questionnaire to fill out

00:29:40.760 --> 00:29:44.090 align:middle line:84%
what I would like to learn,
what sports I would play,

00:29:44.090 --> 00:29:44.880 align:middle line:90%
and all of that.

00:29:44.880 --> 00:29:46.820 align:middle line:84%
And they wanted
to pay everything.

00:29:46.820 --> 00:29:49.340 align:middle line:84%
I had nothing to do,
just to go to the school.

00:29:49.340 --> 00:29:50.450 align:middle line:90%
Like a scholarship.

00:29:50.450 --> 00:29:51.500 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:29:51.500 --> 00:29:57.350 align:middle line:84%
And I wanted-- at
the time, I decided

00:29:57.350 --> 00:30:02.030 align:middle line:90%
to be an engineer, engineering.

00:30:02.030 --> 00:30:03.110 align:middle line:90%
I wrote back.

00:30:03.110 --> 00:30:04.370 align:middle line:90%
They accepted me.

00:30:04.370 --> 00:30:08.930 align:middle line:84%
They even sent me home a ticket
and exactly how-- directions

00:30:08.930 --> 00:30:12.620 align:middle line:84%
how to go, where to stand, to
arrive, who will wait for me,

00:30:12.620 --> 00:30:16.310 align:middle line:84%
and what clothing to bring with
me for sports and football,

00:30:16.310 --> 00:30:19.610 align:middle line:84%
and even an instrument, a
musical instrument, to play,

00:30:19.610 --> 00:30:21.020 align:middle line:90%
and all of that.

00:30:21.020 --> 00:30:24.890 align:middle line:84%
My grandmother from my father's
side, my father's mother,

00:30:24.890 --> 00:30:27.800 align:middle line:90%
she went to the rabbi.

00:30:27.800 --> 00:30:30.800 align:middle line:84%
And she said to the rabbi, this
and this is going to happen.

00:30:30.800 --> 00:30:35.870 align:middle line:84%
My grandson is going
to that kind of school.

00:30:35.870 --> 00:30:40.580 align:middle line:84%
The rabbi says, gevalt, he's
going to be eating treyf.

00:30:40.580 --> 00:30:43.820 align:middle line:84%
He's not going to be able
to go to temple on Shabbos.

00:30:43.820 --> 00:30:47.305 align:middle line:84%
And he's not going to be
able to put on the tefillin.

00:30:47.305 --> 00:30:48.680 align:middle line:84%
He's not going to
be able to pray

00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:50.240 align:middle line:90%
in the morning and the evening.

00:30:50.240 --> 00:30:52.265 align:middle line:90%
He discouraged her.

00:30:52.265 --> 00:30:57.590 align:middle line:84%
And that kind of-- she came home
all fired up against my father

00:30:57.590 --> 00:30:59.060 align:middle line:84%
and especially
against my mother.

00:30:59.060 --> 00:31:01.280 align:middle line:84%
Because my mother was
a very modern woman.

00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:04.430 align:middle line:90%
And what are you going?

00:31:04.430 --> 00:31:06.680 align:middle line:90%
So my father couldn't bear it.

00:31:06.680 --> 00:31:08.010 align:middle line:90%
He had to cancel it.

00:31:08.010 --> 00:31:11.800 align:middle line:84%
So in this kind of environment,
in that kind of circumstance,

00:31:11.800 --> 00:31:14.500 align:middle line:84%
I'm trying to give
you the concept of.

00:31:14.500 --> 00:31:19.720 align:middle line:84%
Now, we teenagers who were
organized in the Zionist

00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:25.330 align:middle line:84%
movement, we felt
something is to happen.

00:31:25.330 --> 00:31:29.240 align:middle line:84%
But we had no, so to
speak, leadership.

00:31:29.240 --> 00:31:32.110 align:middle line:84%
And as you will see
further, you will understand

00:31:32.110 --> 00:31:33.520 align:middle line:90%
what I'm talking about.

00:31:33.520 --> 00:31:37.240 align:middle line:84%
Because it's hard to
explain how the events went.

00:31:37.240 --> 00:31:39.080 align:middle line:84%
We knew something
is about to happen.

00:31:39.080 --> 00:31:43.150 align:middle line:84%
We tried to organize the younger
generation already together

00:31:43.150 --> 00:31:45.430 align:middle line:90%
as much as possible.

00:31:45.430 --> 00:31:46.960 align:middle line:90%
But everything was closed.

00:31:46.960 --> 00:31:52.360 align:middle line:84%
We could not move out because
we were framed in, boarded in.

00:31:52.360 --> 00:31:53.890 align:middle line:90%
We were already Hungary.

00:31:53.890 --> 00:31:56.530 align:middle line:84%
So we could not go
back to Czechoslovakia

00:31:56.530 --> 00:31:58.720 align:middle line:84%
because there is
already trouble.

00:31:58.720 --> 00:32:01.000 align:middle line:84%
Romanian, all the
borders were closed.

00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:03.890 align:middle line:84%
And if anybody was caught,
he was shipped back.

00:32:03.890 --> 00:32:06.070 align:middle line:90%
On the other hand was Germany.

00:32:06.070 --> 00:32:08.245 align:middle line:90%
Germany was already in Poland.

00:32:08.245 --> 00:32:12.120 align:middle line:84%
And Germany was already
in Czechoslovakia.

00:32:12.120 --> 00:32:13.040 align:middle line:90%
So what's left?

00:32:13.040 --> 00:32:14.010 align:middle line:90%
We couldn't go nowhere.

00:32:14.010 --> 00:32:17.227 align:middle line:84%
The only place to go was
Romania or Yugoslavia.

00:32:17.227 --> 00:32:19.310 align:middle line:84%
And Yugoslavia, you couldn't
go because Yugoslavia

00:32:19.310 --> 00:32:22.890 align:middle line:84%
had their own problems at the
same time as we had in Hungary.

00:32:22.890 --> 00:32:23.390 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:32:23.390 --> 00:32:27.470 align:middle line:84%
Let's talk about what happened
to you as the war progressed.

00:32:27.470 --> 00:32:29.810 align:middle line:84%
As the war
progressed, and made--

00:32:29.810 --> 00:32:31.580 align:middle line:90%
everything went.

00:32:31.580 --> 00:32:36.890 align:middle line:90%
In 1942, I was out of school.

00:32:36.890 --> 00:32:38.160 align:middle line:90%
I had to leave school.

00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:40.430 align:middle line:90%
I couldn't do anything.

00:32:40.430 --> 00:32:44.270 align:middle line:90%
Food became a problem, scarce.

00:32:44.270 --> 00:32:47.390 align:middle line:90%
Black market started.

00:32:47.390 --> 00:32:48.740 align:middle line:90%
Your father wasn't working.

00:32:48.740 --> 00:32:49.490 align:middle line:90%
No, he wasn't.

00:32:49.490 --> 00:32:49.610 align:middle line:90%
The business was--

00:32:49.610 --> 00:32:50.930 align:middle line:90%
Everybody was just staying home.

00:32:50.930 --> 00:32:51.430 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yes.

00:32:51.430 --> 00:32:52.340 align:middle line:90%
We all staying home.

00:32:52.340 --> 00:32:52.700 align:middle line:90%
Everything was taken away.

00:32:52.700 --> 00:32:54.200 align:middle line:84%
And you were afraid
to move, almost.

00:32:54.200 --> 00:32:56.790 align:middle line:84%
Business didn't
existed-- nonexistent.

00:32:56.790 --> 00:32:59.600 align:middle line:90%


00:32:59.600 --> 00:33:02.540 align:middle line:84%
A Jew could not do
any kind of work.

00:33:02.540 --> 00:33:05.300 align:middle line:90%
He had no job, no businesses.

00:33:05.300 --> 00:33:07.520 align:middle line:84%
And then things
starting to go bad.

00:33:07.520 --> 00:33:13.030 align:middle line:84%
There was a lot of problems in
the Jewish community because

00:33:13.030 --> 00:33:18.070 align:middle line:84%
of the daily needs and
for the daily survival.

00:33:18.070 --> 00:33:22.690 align:middle line:84%
So to speak, the well-to-do
Jews had to open their pockets

00:33:22.690 --> 00:33:24.953 align:middle line:84%
and do what they
can to help others--

00:33:24.953 --> 00:33:25.870 align:middle line:90%
To help others, right.

00:33:25.870 --> 00:33:27.880 align:middle line:90%
--more than in the usual way.

00:33:27.880 --> 00:33:31.190 align:middle line:84%
And I do remember my father
selling all kind of things

00:33:31.190 --> 00:33:34.780 align:middle line:84%
in order not only for us--
to support us or the rest

00:33:34.780 --> 00:33:36.825 align:middle line:84%
of the family,
but other people--

00:33:36.825 --> 00:33:37.450 align:middle line:90%
To help others.

00:33:37.450 --> 00:33:39.160 align:middle line:84%
--others who we knew
and all of that.

00:33:39.160 --> 00:33:39.295 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:33:39.295 --> 00:33:40.090 align:middle line:90%
Then they came in.

00:33:40.090 --> 00:33:42.100 align:middle line:90%
And were you taken away?

00:33:42.100 --> 00:33:44.140 align:middle line:90%
As a family, were you moved?

00:33:44.140 --> 00:33:47.020 align:middle line:84%
Then here comes a little
bit of a different--

00:33:47.020 --> 00:33:51.630 align:middle line:90%
my life story is a unusual one.

00:33:51.630 --> 00:33:52.130 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:33:52.130 --> 00:33:52.963 align:middle line:90%
That's what we want.

00:33:52.963 --> 00:33:56.237 align:middle line:84%
And my life story is not
the every survivor story.

00:33:56.237 --> 00:33:57.070 align:middle line:90%
That doesn't matter.

00:33:57.070 --> 00:33:58.660 align:middle line:90%
We're interested in your story.

00:33:58.660 --> 00:34:02.892 align:middle line:84%
My story has a different, as
you will see as I keep going.

00:34:02.892 --> 00:34:03.392 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:34:03.392 --> 00:34:04.810 align:middle line:90%
Let's go on.

00:34:04.810 --> 00:34:09.310 align:middle line:90%
1943 is approaching.

00:34:09.310 --> 00:34:12.440 align:middle line:84%
We had a meeting at the
Zionist organization.

00:34:12.440 --> 00:34:17.900 align:middle line:84%
And there was rumors
that for our hometown,

00:34:17.900 --> 00:34:19.639 align:middle line:90%
there will be four--

00:34:19.639 --> 00:34:22.310 align:middle line:84%
at the time, we
called it certificates

00:34:22.310 --> 00:34:26.540 align:middle line:90%
available to go to Palestine.

00:34:26.540 --> 00:34:28.040 align:middle line:90%
And this--

00:34:28.040 --> 00:34:29.210 align:middle line:90%
Who was issuing these?

00:34:29.210 --> 00:34:33.980 align:middle line:84%
They used to be issued from
the British and from Palestine.

00:34:33.980 --> 00:34:35.389 align:middle line:90%
And to Hungary used to--

00:34:35.389 --> 00:34:37.699 align:middle line:90%
came that Hungary will release--

00:34:37.699 --> 00:34:39.770 align:middle line:84%
they will be permitted
to leave, at the time,

00:34:39.770 --> 00:34:43.400 align:middle line:84%
if I remember correctly, there
was 150 Jews, young people.

00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:45.540 align:middle line:84%
My hometown received
from the 100

00:34:45.540 --> 00:34:47.690 align:middle line:84%
the quota of four
to be released.

00:34:47.690 --> 00:34:49.969 align:middle line:90%
I understand.

00:34:49.969 --> 00:34:56.989 align:middle line:84%
The boys' decision was made that
I will be one of them in going.

00:34:56.989 --> 00:35:01.100 align:middle line:84%
I went to Budapest, discussed
with the leadership there.

00:35:01.100 --> 00:35:02.210 align:middle line:90%
And they said, yes.

00:35:02.210 --> 00:35:05.510 align:middle line:84%
Do you want me to
go for the qualities

00:35:05.510 --> 00:35:08.300 align:middle line:84%
that I possess of the
languages I possess that I may

00:35:08.300 --> 00:35:11.060 align:middle line:90%
be in a need for a later date?

00:35:11.060 --> 00:35:12.750 align:middle line:84%
We don't know what's
going to happen.

00:35:12.750 --> 00:35:16.190 align:middle line:84%
And they are predicting--
they feel that I should go.

00:35:16.190 --> 00:35:17.480 align:middle line:90%
This was 1942?

00:35:17.480 --> 00:35:22.040 align:middle line:84%
That's 1942, close
to the end of 1942.

00:35:22.040 --> 00:35:24.170 align:middle line:84%
Or it's late fall, in
the beginning of fall,

00:35:24.170 --> 00:35:25.400 align:middle line:90%
let's put it this way.

00:35:25.400 --> 00:35:26.600 align:middle line:90%
I came home.

00:35:26.600 --> 00:35:29.270 align:middle line:84%
And I said, I'm going
to start packing.

00:35:29.270 --> 00:35:33.440 align:middle line:84%
I'm going to leave
for Palestine.

00:35:33.440 --> 00:35:37.370 align:middle line:84%
And rumors had it that
there was only four.

00:35:37.370 --> 00:35:39.620 align:middle line:90%
And everybody wanted to get out.

00:35:39.620 --> 00:35:42.200 align:middle line:84%
My mother-- we sit
down one evening.

00:35:42.200 --> 00:35:47.033 align:middle line:84%
And my mother says
to me, are you fair?

00:35:47.033 --> 00:35:47.700 align:middle line:90%
I looked at her.

00:35:47.700 --> 00:35:49.242 align:middle line:84%
And I says, Mother,
what do you mean?

00:35:49.242 --> 00:35:52.340 align:middle line:84%
And she says to me-- these
are the words what she said.

00:35:52.340 --> 00:35:54.290 align:middle line:90%
After all, she says--

00:35:54.290 --> 00:35:56.930 align:middle line:84%
I used to call me the
macher, my macher.

00:35:56.930 --> 00:35:59.540 align:middle line:84%
My mother used to call
me-- here is my macher.

00:35:59.540 --> 00:36:00.470 align:middle line:90%
The big man.

00:36:00.470 --> 00:36:01.130 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:36:01.130 --> 00:36:04.100 align:middle line:84%
So after all, you're
the big macher.

00:36:04.100 --> 00:36:05.750 align:middle line:84%
She says, you're the
guy who is running

00:36:05.750 --> 00:36:06.880 align:middle line:90%
around all over the place.

00:36:06.880 --> 00:36:10.040 align:middle line:90%
And you're the-- why do you--

00:36:10.040 --> 00:36:12.560 align:middle line:84%
it will look like you're
taking for yourself.

00:36:12.560 --> 00:36:15.200 align:middle line:84%
How about giving it
to somebody else?

00:36:15.200 --> 00:36:18.140 align:middle line:84%
After all, you're
a shtetl leader.

00:36:18.140 --> 00:36:20.400 align:middle line:90%
So it doesn't look good.

00:36:20.400 --> 00:36:22.740 align:middle line:84%
It will look like you
were taking yourself.

00:36:22.740 --> 00:36:25.610 align:middle line:84%
So I says, how about if
I give it to my sister,

00:36:25.610 --> 00:36:27.530 align:middle line:84%
to my younger sister,
and let her go?

00:36:27.530 --> 00:36:32.450 align:middle line:84%
She says, no, you give
it to somebody else.

00:36:32.450 --> 00:36:34.610 align:middle line:84%
At the time, I didn't
click, but later on,

00:36:34.610 --> 00:36:36.410 align:middle line:84%
the downtime, in--
later on in years,

00:36:36.410 --> 00:36:38.090 align:middle line:84%
that she didn't
want us to leave.

00:36:38.090 --> 00:36:39.380 align:middle line:90%
We wanted to stick together.

00:36:39.380 --> 00:36:39.690 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:40.295 align:middle line:90%
Keep the family together.

00:36:40.295 --> 00:36:40.910 align:middle line:90%
So anyhow.

00:36:40.910 --> 00:36:44.450 align:middle line:84%
But the paradox of it
is the ones who left,

00:36:44.450 --> 00:36:45.275 align:middle line:90%
they all survived.

00:36:45.275 --> 00:36:49.050 align:middle line:84%
And they are in
Israel till this day.

00:36:49.050 --> 00:36:53.360 align:middle line:84%
So I gave it away to somebody
else and the four of them.

00:36:53.360 --> 00:36:57.450 align:middle line:84%
And they left for Israel, for
then, at the time, Palestine.

00:36:57.450 --> 00:36:57.980 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:36:57.980 --> 00:36:59.510 align:middle line:90%
So then what happened to you?

00:36:59.510 --> 00:37:03.170 align:middle line:90%
Then I stayed home.

00:37:03.170 --> 00:37:07.160 align:middle line:84%
I had to go around and
make every day problems

00:37:07.160 --> 00:37:10.980 align:middle line:84%
to accumulating-- to see for
the everyday daily survival.

00:37:10.980 --> 00:37:11.850 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:37:11.850 --> 00:37:15.750 align:middle line:84%
And my headache was not
only for myself already.

00:37:15.750 --> 00:37:18.750 align:middle line:84%
Because there were a lot of
older people who their kids got

00:37:18.750 --> 00:37:21.390 align:middle line:84%
stuck all over the world
in different places.

00:37:21.390 --> 00:37:23.860 align:middle line:84%
And they could not have
any-- so in other words,

00:37:23.860 --> 00:37:27.930 align:middle line:84%
we had to get busy to help
everybody in the way we could.

00:37:27.930 --> 00:37:32.393 align:middle line:84%
In '43, things
starting to go worse.

00:37:32.393 --> 00:37:33.060 align:middle line:90%
You were still--

00:37:33.060 --> 00:37:33.768 align:middle line:90%
We're still home.

00:37:33.768 --> 00:37:35.107 align:middle line:90%
--19 years-- 18-19 years old.

00:37:35.107 --> 00:37:36.440 align:middle line:90%
You had a lot of responsibility.

00:37:36.440 --> 00:37:36.675 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:37:36.675 --> 00:37:37.380 align:middle line:90%
I still-- responsibilities.

00:37:37.380 --> 00:37:37.950 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:37:37.950 --> 00:37:39.690 align:middle line:84%
In other words,
I realized, I had

00:37:39.690 --> 00:37:43.440 align:middle line:84%
to grow up overnight,
simple fact.

00:37:43.440 --> 00:37:46.920 align:middle line:84%
Then we were taken
to the ghettos.

00:37:46.920 --> 00:37:49.300 align:middle line:84%
In 1943, we have been
taken to ghettos.

00:37:49.300 --> 00:37:49.800 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:52.620 align:middle line:84%
Now, tell me, the ghettos--
you mean, in your own town?

00:37:52.620 --> 00:37:54.630 align:middle line:90%
Let me explain what a ghetto is.

00:37:54.630 --> 00:38:00.060 align:middle line:84%
Ghetto is-- of course,
Germans came in already,

00:38:00.060 --> 00:38:03.420 align:middle line:84%
occupied the entire section,
the Carpathian link.

00:38:03.420 --> 00:38:06.030 align:middle line:84%
And it was under occupation
with the Germans,

00:38:06.030 --> 00:38:07.460 align:middle line:90%
but also Hungarians.

00:38:07.460 --> 00:38:13.610 align:middle line:90%


00:38:13.610 --> 00:38:17.230 align:middle line:84%
The first-- right away, the
first thing what they did is,

00:38:17.230 --> 00:38:21.770 align:middle line:84%
in creating the ghetto, is they
going in a section of the town.

00:38:21.770 --> 00:38:25.970 align:middle line:84%
Mostly, they looked the sections
where Jews were concentrated.

00:38:25.970 --> 00:38:29.120 align:middle line:84%
And they clean out the
all surrounding area,

00:38:29.120 --> 00:38:30.660 align:middle line:90%
all of the houses.

00:38:30.660 --> 00:38:33.415 align:middle line:84%
If any Gentiles,
they move them out

00:38:33.415 --> 00:38:34.790 align:middle line:84%
and they give them
another house,

00:38:34.790 --> 00:38:37.970 align:middle line:84%
of a Jewish home or a
Jewish house somewhere else.

00:38:37.970 --> 00:38:42.290 align:middle line:84%
Then they bring in all the
Jews from that hometown,

00:38:42.290 --> 00:38:46.370 align:middle line:84%
from the whole town, to that
particular designated area.

00:38:46.370 --> 00:38:48.090 align:middle line:90%
And they seal it off.

00:38:48.090 --> 00:38:49.880 align:middle line:90%
And this is-- we moved in.

00:38:49.880 --> 00:38:50.750 align:middle line:90%
We had to move in.

00:38:50.750 --> 00:38:52.850 align:middle line:90%
We were five in our family--

00:38:52.850 --> 00:38:55.640 align:middle line:90%
I mean, let's see--

00:38:55.640 --> 00:38:56.852 align:middle line:90%
there was one boy, four--

00:38:56.852 --> 00:38:57.935 align:middle line:90%
we were six in the family.

00:38:57.935 --> 00:39:00.305 align:middle line:90%
And so we had one room.

00:39:00.305 --> 00:39:02.617 align:middle line:84%
Well, there were four
children-- five children--

00:39:02.617 --> 00:39:03.200 align:middle line:90%
Five children.

00:39:03.200 --> 00:39:03.800 align:middle line:90%
--and your parents.

00:39:03.800 --> 00:39:04.310 align:middle line:90%
My parents.

00:39:04.310 --> 00:39:06.170 align:middle line:90%
So there were seven.

00:39:06.170 --> 00:39:06.800 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:39:06.800 --> 00:39:08.880 align:middle line:84%
Your mother, and father,
and the seven children.

00:39:08.880 --> 00:39:09.380 align:middle line:90%
Yes, seven.

00:39:09.380 --> 00:39:10.460 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, four girls.

00:39:10.460 --> 00:39:12.750 align:middle line:84%
I mean, and the five
children-- four girls and you.

00:39:12.750 --> 00:39:14.393 align:middle line:84%
But also, my
grandmother was with us.

00:39:14.393 --> 00:39:15.435 align:middle line:90%
So that there were eight.

00:39:15.435 --> 00:39:15.977 align:middle line:90%
Eight people.

00:39:15.977 --> 00:39:20.064 align:middle line:84%
We had to move in-- eight
of us had to move into a--

00:39:20.064 --> 00:39:22.080 align:middle line:90%
to a one room.

00:39:22.080 --> 00:39:22.800 align:middle line:90%
In a home.

00:39:22.800 --> 00:39:23.328 align:middle line:90%
In a house.

00:39:23.328 --> 00:39:24.120 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, it's a house.

00:39:24.120 --> 00:39:25.200 align:middle line:84%
But you had one room was
your living quarters.

00:39:25.200 --> 00:39:26.033 align:middle line:90%
And we got one room.

00:39:26.033 --> 00:39:28.265 align:middle line:84%
And another room was another
family, and a third room

00:39:28.265 --> 00:39:28.890 align:middle line:90%
a third family.

00:39:28.890 --> 00:39:29.432 align:middle line:90%
I understand.

00:39:29.432 --> 00:39:32.310 align:middle line:84%
We were about four or
five families together.

00:39:32.310 --> 00:39:33.810 align:middle line:90%
Were these people you knew?

00:39:33.810 --> 00:39:35.400 align:middle line:90%
People from-- yes, from--

00:39:35.400 --> 00:39:36.120 align:middle line:84%
Jewish people from
your community, right.

00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:37.578 align:middle line:84%
--Jewish people
from the community,

00:39:37.578 --> 00:39:40.800 align:middle line:84%
from the town, what
we knew very well.

00:39:40.800 --> 00:39:44.400 align:middle line:84%
And of course, we
were-- the way it

00:39:44.400 --> 00:39:49.050 align:middle line:84%
was conducted is you
come in, say, hey,

00:39:49.050 --> 00:39:50.610 align:middle line:90%
you pack tomorrow morning.

00:39:50.610 --> 00:39:51.540 align:middle line:90%
You are leaving.

00:39:51.540 --> 00:39:53.535 align:middle line:84%
You can take with you
this, take blankets,

00:39:53.535 --> 00:39:57.030 align:middle line:84%
get a little bit food to last
you for a couple of days.

00:39:57.030 --> 00:39:59.370 align:middle line:90%
You cannot take your jewelry.

00:39:59.370 --> 00:40:02.610 align:middle line:84%
You cannot take this, fancy
stuff, coats, and that,

00:40:02.610 --> 00:40:04.485 align:middle line:90%
just regular clothing.

00:40:04.485 --> 00:40:07.650 align:middle line:90%


00:40:07.650 --> 00:40:09.870 align:middle line:90%
And that's the way it happened.

00:40:09.870 --> 00:40:11.010 align:middle line:90%
Well, how did you--

00:40:11.010 --> 00:40:13.050 align:middle line:84%
what difficulties did
you encounter there?

00:40:13.050 --> 00:40:16.020 align:middle line:84%
Who supplied you with
food in the ghetto?

00:40:16.020 --> 00:40:19.170 align:middle line:84%
At that time, we are
moving in the-- we are just

00:40:19.170 --> 00:40:20.800 align:middle line:90%
moving in in the ghetto.

00:40:20.800 --> 00:40:23.310 align:middle line:90%
And we took some food with us.

00:40:23.310 --> 00:40:28.890 align:middle line:84%
And by being in the
ghetto, I remember

00:40:28.890 --> 00:40:33.750 align:middle line:84%
that we managed to get
a meeting together.

00:40:33.750 --> 00:40:36.750 align:middle line:84%
And we decided, we are going
to take the wagons, horse

00:40:36.750 --> 00:40:38.340 align:middle line:90%
and buggy wagons.

00:40:38.340 --> 00:40:40.150 align:middle line:84%
And we'll go from
house to house.

00:40:40.150 --> 00:40:43.710 align:middle line:84%
And whatever food is left
in the Jewish families,

00:40:43.710 --> 00:40:45.660 align:middle line:90%
we'll put it in that wagon.

00:40:45.660 --> 00:40:47.328 align:middle line:84%
And we'll bring it
in in the ghetto.

00:40:47.328 --> 00:40:47.870 align:middle line:90%
And this is--

00:40:47.870 --> 00:40:50.700 align:middle line:84%
Oh, you were permitted to go
out during the day to do this?

00:40:50.700 --> 00:40:51.990 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:40:51.990 --> 00:40:55.530 align:middle line:84%
This is still the same
process as is moving out.

00:40:55.530 --> 00:40:58.110 align:middle line:84%
We had three, four
days to do that.

00:40:58.110 --> 00:41:01.300 align:middle line:84%
In the period of those three,
four days, this is what we did.

00:41:01.300 --> 00:41:02.430 align:middle line:90%
So we went out.

00:41:02.430 --> 00:41:04.200 align:middle line:90%
And we brought from every house.

00:41:04.200 --> 00:41:05.430 align:middle line:90%
We went in in every house.

00:41:05.430 --> 00:41:08.310 align:middle line:84%
What we found food,
we put it in--

00:41:08.310 --> 00:41:11.250 align:middle line:84%
butter, oil, cheese,
cream cheese, flour,

00:41:11.250 --> 00:41:13.230 align:middle line:84%
whatever-- sugar,
whatever we found,

00:41:13.230 --> 00:41:14.400 align:middle line:90%
we put everything together.

00:41:14.400 --> 00:41:15.720 align:middle line:90%
We brought it in the ghetto.

00:41:15.720 --> 00:41:18.450 align:middle line:84%
And then we had
another group who

00:41:18.450 --> 00:41:19.920 align:middle line:90%
was dividing it, giving out.

00:41:19.920 --> 00:41:23.040 align:middle line:84%
Any family who came and needed
food right away was given.

00:41:23.040 --> 00:41:25.020 align:middle line:84%
Right, right, sort
of community living.

00:41:25.020 --> 00:41:25.620 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:41:25.620 --> 00:41:26.120 align:middle line:90%
And--

00:41:26.120 --> 00:41:29.500 align:middle line:90%


00:41:29.500 --> 00:41:30.000 align:middle line:90%
How long--

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:32.520 align:middle line:84%
--what I didn't
know at the time was

00:41:32.520 --> 00:41:37.080 align:middle line:84%
that the Germans
observed who are

00:41:37.080 --> 00:41:40.590 align:middle line:84%
top machers who
are doing things,

00:41:40.590 --> 00:41:43.620 align:middle line:90%
and who were leading, and so on.

00:41:43.620 --> 00:41:46.410 align:middle line:84%
I didn't know that they
already knew who I am,

00:41:46.410 --> 00:41:48.420 align:middle line:84%
and what I'm doing,
and they observed me.

00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:51.030 align:middle line:90%


00:41:51.030 --> 00:41:53.970 align:middle line:84%
After being in the ghetto, and
every settled down a little

00:41:53.970 --> 00:41:57.150 align:middle line:84%
bit, quieted down, and
everybody was already--

00:41:57.150 --> 00:42:05.580 align:middle line:84%
two days later, one of the
Jewish Judenrat, so to speak,

00:42:05.580 --> 00:42:07.620 align:middle line:90%
came in.

00:42:07.620 --> 00:42:09.360 align:middle line:90%
And he says, Larry--

00:42:09.360 --> 00:42:10.995 align:middle line:90%
my Jewish name was Leibe.

00:42:10.995 --> 00:42:15.630 align:middle line:84%
He says, Leibe, this is
the chief of the Gestapo.

00:42:15.630 --> 00:42:17.520 align:middle line:84%
And the chief-- there
was a big chief.

00:42:17.520 --> 00:42:21.070 align:middle line:84%
He was-- he had a half
a dozen men with him.

00:42:21.070 --> 00:42:22.930 align:middle line:90%
He wants to talk to you.

00:42:22.930 --> 00:42:23.800 align:middle line:90%
It was fine.

00:42:23.800 --> 00:42:25.920 align:middle line:84%
So I came in and
took my hat off.

00:42:25.920 --> 00:42:30.900 align:middle line:84%
So he says to me
now, first question

00:42:30.900 --> 00:42:32.940 align:middle line:90%
is do you speak German?

00:42:32.940 --> 00:42:36.720 align:middle line:90%
So I says, a little bit.

00:42:36.720 --> 00:42:37.537 align:middle line:90%
And he says, OK.

00:42:37.537 --> 00:42:39.120 align:middle line:84%
He says, I'm going
to test you and see

00:42:39.120 --> 00:42:41.310 align:middle line:90%
how little bit you speak.

00:42:41.310 --> 00:42:43.680 align:middle line:84%
And he's asking
me some questions,

00:42:43.680 --> 00:42:46.320 align:middle line:84%
minor questions-- how
many wagons of food

00:42:46.320 --> 00:42:47.760 align:middle line:90%
did you brought in?

00:42:47.760 --> 00:42:50.190 align:middle line:90%
And did you got all of it out?

00:42:50.190 --> 00:42:53.160 align:middle line:84%
And still-- do you think
there's still some left?

00:42:53.160 --> 00:42:57.180 align:middle line:84%
Or can you still get a wagon and
the horses together and get it?

00:42:57.180 --> 00:43:00.720 align:middle line:90%
That kind of good approach.

00:43:00.720 --> 00:43:05.640 align:middle line:84%
And then he says, how many boys
do you have working with you?

00:43:05.640 --> 00:43:07.080 align:middle line:90%
I was naive.

00:43:07.080 --> 00:43:08.755 align:middle line:84%
I didn't know what
he is shooting--

00:43:08.755 --> 00:43:09.630 align:middle line:90%
Why he's asking this.

00:43:09.630 --> 00:43:10.990 align:middle line:90%
--what he is shooting for.

00:43:10.990 --> 00:43:12.520 align:middle line:90%
So I gave him all the answers.

00:43:12.520 --> 00:43:16.190 align:middle line:84%
And he says, well, your
German is pretty good.

00:43:16.190 --> 00:43:21.700 align:middle line:84%
So he says, go ahead and
do what you have to do.

00:43:21.700 --> 00:43:23.990 align:middle line:84%
Bring in more food
and all of that.

00:43:23.990 --> 00:43:27.580 align:middle line:84%
That lasted for
approximately a good week.

00:43:27.580 --> 00:43:32.560 align:middle line:84%
Afterwards, the week
is over, my father

00:43:32.560 --> 00:43:37.940 align:middle line:84%
knew another guy, a non-Jew who
was working for the Germans,

00:43:37.940 --> 00:43:42.490 align:middle line:90%
was a Hungarian policeman.

00:43:42.490 --> 00:43:45.520 align:middle line:84%
But my father used
to give him money,

00:43:45.520 --> 00:43:49.550 align:middle line:84%
buy him drinks-- not
years back from before.

00:43:49.550 --> 00:43:51.820 align:middle line:90%
So he was standing guard.

00:43:51.820 --> 00:43:52.940 align:middle line:90%
They are walking around.

00:43:52.940 --> 00:43:57.370 align:middle line:84%
So my father calls him over and
says, hey, he says, be a pal.

00:43:57.370 --> 00:44:00.760 align:middle line:84%
Let me cash in a little bit
on you after all those years.

00:44:00.760 --> 00:44:04.340 align:middle line:84%
Look, he says, see what you
can find out and let me know.

00:44:04.340 --> 00:44:06.868 align:middle line:90%
Says OK.

00:44:06.868 --> 00:44:08.990 align:middle line:84%
And one day, he comes
over to my father.

00:44:08.990 --> 00:44:13.370 align:middle line:84%
And he says, listen, there
is an order-- the Germans

00:44:13.370 --> 00:44:17.480 align:middle line:84%
them self could not come in the
camp to arrest or take anybody.

00:44:17.480 --> 00:44:18.540 align:middle line:90%
The ghetto, you mean?

00:44:18.540 --> 00:44:19.040 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:44:19.040 --> 00:44:22.520 align:middle line:84%
You had to have the
Hungarians to come in.

00:44:22.520 --> 00:44:25.400 align:middle line:84%
He says to me that
listen, there is an order

00:44:25.400 --> 00:44:30.890 align:middle line:84%
to take in your son and the
rest of the boys, the names

00:44:30.890 --> 00:44:36.080 align:middle line:84%
of another bunch of teenagers,
a whole bunch of young people.

00:44:36.080 --> 00:44:38.120 align:middle line:90%
My father heard this.

00:44:38.120 --> 00:44:40.250 align:middle line:90%
He got busy.

00:44:40.250 --> 00:44:42.770 align:middle line:84%
Till this day, I don't
know how he managed.

00:44:42.770 --> 00:44:47.720 align:middle line:84%
But I got-- we used to call it
a [NON-ENGLISH],, which means--

00:44:47.720 --> 00:44:56.720 align:middle line:84%
it's a-- from the
army, they call you.

00:44:56.720 --> 00:44:59.718 align:middle line:84%
In other words, you have
been recruited to the army--

00:44:59.718 --> 00:45:00.260 align:middle line:90%
I understand.

00:45:00.260 --> 00:45:02.060 align:middle line:90%
--to the Hungarian Army.

00:45:02.060 --> 00:45:05.720 align:middle line:84%
And I had a piece
of paper by saying

00:45:05.720 --> 00:45:08.270 align:middle line:84%
that I have been recruited
by the Hungarian Army

00:45:08.270 --> 00:45:10.920 align:middle line:84%
to report here, and here, and
here at that and that day--

00:45:10.920 --> 00:45:11.420 align:middle line:90%
A call-up

00:45:11.420 --> 00:45:13.010 align:middle line:90%
--to call up to duty.

00:45:13.010 --> 00:45:14.420 align:middle line:90%
Right, call to duty, right.

00:45:14.420 --> 00:45:18.270 align:middle line:84%
Well, if you had this, there
was nobody anything can do.

00:45:18.270 --> 00:45:20.840 align:middle line:84%
You just have to go out,
and pack, and leave.

00:45:20.840 --> 00:45:22.250 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:45:22.250 --> 00:45:24.660 align:middle line:84%
So that's how you stayed out
of their hands that time.

00:45:24.660 --> 00:45:25.160 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:45:25.160 --> 00:45:25.760 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:29.330 align:middle line:90%
But my call was two weeks.

00:45:29.330 --> 00:45:31.670 align:middle line:90%
I still had two weeks' time.

00:45:31.670 --> 00:45:34.218 align:middle line:84%
Well, was this a
legitimate thing?

00:45:34.218 --> 00:45:34.760 align:middle line:90%
A legitimate.

00:45:34.760 --> 00:45:35.150 align:middle line:90%
That's everything.

00:45:35.150 --> 00:45:36.875 align:middle line:84%
Oh, I thought he
maybe paid somebody.

00:45:36.875 --> 00:45:38.013 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yeah, he had to pay it.

00:45:38.013 --> 00:45:38.930 align:middle line:90%
But it was legitimate.

00:45:38.930 --> 00:45:40.520 align:middle line:84%
Oh, but it was
legitimate, whether you

00:45:40.520 --> 00:45:42.560 align:middle line:84%
should go into the army
then go to the Germans.

00:45:42.560 --> 00:45:42.800 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:45:42.800 --> 00:45:43.300 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:45:43.300 --> 00:45:44.540 align:middle line:90%
That was legitimate, yes.

00:45:44.540 --> 00:45:46.610 align:middle line:90%
But it was bribery.

00:45:46.610 --> 00:45:48.440 align:middle line:90%
But it was legitimate.

00:45:48.440 --> 00:45:50.120 align:middle line:90%
But it was two weeks later.

00:45:50.120 --> 00:45:51.810 align:middle line:90%
I still had two weeks' time.

00:45:51.810 --> 00:45:54.650 align:middle line:84%
So in order-- we
tried to figure out

00:45:54.650 --> 00:45:56.960 align:middle line:84%
for them what to do
in those two weeks.

00:45:56.960 --> 00:46:02.120 align:middle line:84%
Well, rumors got to us that
there are still some papers

00:46:02.120 --> 00:46:05.420 align:middle line:90%
available in Budapest.

00:46:05.420 --> 00:46:07.070 align:middle line:84%
See, Budapest was
not ghetto yet.

00:46:07.070 --> 00:46:08.660 align:middle line:90%
We don't know at the time.

00:46:08.660 --> 00:46:11.210 align:middle line:90%
We don't know what's going on.

00:46:11.210 --> 00:46:12.020 align:middle line:90%
But we don't--

00:46:12.020 --> 00:46:12.730 align:middle line:90%
Papers for what?

00:46:12.730 --> 00:46:13.730 align:middle line:90%
For Palestine, you mean?

00:46:13.730 --> 00:46:15.740 align:middle line:84%
Not for Palestine, but
to other countries,

00:46:15.740 --> 00:46:17.090 align:middle line:90%
to be able to get away.

00:46:17.090 --> 00:46:17.630 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:46:17.630 --> 00:46:22.970 align:middle line:84%
That was the time that we
didn't know what's happening.

00:46:22.970 --> 00:46:26.465 align:middle line:84%
So since I didn't look Jewish,
I could get away with it.

00:46:26.465 --> 00:46:28.340 align:middle line:84%
And not looking like a
Jew, I got dressed up,

00:46:28.340 --> 00:46:30.440 align:middle line:90%
and I went to Budapest.

00:46:30.440 --> 00:46:33.650 align:middle line:84%
I met with my people
who I knew from before.

00:46:33.650 --> 00:46:36.170 align:middle line:84%
And they all said, it's
trouble everywhere.

00:46:36.170 --> 00:46:41.210 align:middle line:84%
And they are expecting somebody
to arrive from Palestine

00:46:41.210 --> 00:46:45.980 align:middle line:84%
pretty soon, who will
instruct what to do.

00:46:45.980 --> 00:46:49.545 align:middle line:90%
And therefore, nothing I can do.

00:46:49.545 --> 00:46:51.170 align:middle line:84%
The only thing they
can help me is they

00:46:51.170 --> 00:46:52.760 align:middle line:90%
have two pieces of paper.

00:46:52.760 --> 00:46:55.010 align:middle line:84%
And they don't know
how much it will work

00:46:55.010 --> 00:46:57.440 align:middle line:84%
and how much not
that somebody will

00:46:57.440 --> 00:46:59.690 align:middle line:84%
be able to go to
Romania, to escape,

00:46:59.690 --> 00:47:02.330 align:middle line:84%
that he will be able to cross
the border and go into Romania.

00:47:02.330 --> 00:47:03.705 align:middle line:84%
You preferred--
you didn't really

00:47:03.705 --> 00:47:05.690 align:middle line:84%
want to go to the
Hungarian Army.

00:47:05.690 --> 00:47:07.010 align:middle line:90%
I'm still home there.

00:47:07.010 --> 00:47:10.160 align:middle line:90%
I still have this.

00:47:10.160 --> 00:47:12.530 align:middle line:84%
So they didn't know
what to tell me.

00:47:12.530 --> 00:47:14.660 align:middle line:84%
They said, we do
the best we can.

00:47:14.660 --> 00:47:16.730 align:middle line:90%
Try and stay in touch.

00:47:16.730 --> 00:47:18.170 align:middle line:90%
And let's see what happens.

00:47:18.170 --> 00:47:20.330 align:middle line:84%
Because we could
not use telephones.

00:47:20.330 --> 00:47:22.070 align:middle line:90%
We could have no communications.

00:47:22.070 --> 00:47:24.260 align:middle line:90%
It had to-- excuse me.

00:47:24.260 --> 00:47:27.690 align:middle line:84%
It had to be on
a personal level.

00:47:27.690 --> 00:47:31.250 align:middle line:84%
So nothing accomplishing, I
took those two pieces of paper.

00:47:31.250 --> 00:47:34.190 align:middle line:84%
They were like passports,
two pieces of passport.

00:47:34.190 --> 00:47:35.510 align:middle line:90%
I came home.

00:47:35.510 --> 00:47:39.080 align:middle line:84%
And we had a meeting, who
should be the two to go.

00:47:39.080 --> 00:47:42.320 align:middle line:84%
So I wanted one of
them to be my sister.

00:47:42.320 --> 00:47:46.730 align:middle line:84%
All the thing we had to do
is to put the picture on it.

00:47:46.730 --> 00:47:48.770 align:middle line:84%
And I had a little
piece of rubber

00:47:48.770 --> 00:47:51.090 align:middle line:90%
to give it a stamp to make it--

00:47:51.090 --> 00:47:51.590 align:middle line:90%
Official.

00:47:51.590 --> 00:47:52.280 align:middle line:90%
--have official.

00:47:52.280 --> 00:47:54.900 align:middle line:90%
Anything else was-- you know.

00:47:54.900 --> 00:48:02.540 align:middle line:84%
So they said, no, we'll
send another couple.

00:48:02.540 --> 00:48:04.250 align:middle line:84%
There was a young
couple who just got

00:48:04.250 --> 00:48:06.320 align:middle line:90%
married a couple of years ago.

00:48:06.320 --> 00:48:08.480 align:middle line:90%
And we decided for them to go.

00:48:08.480 --> 00:48:09.440 align:middle line:90%
And we gave it to them.

00:48:09.440 --> 00:48:10.490 align:middle line:90%
And they went to Romania.

00:48:10.490 --> 00:48:12.220 align:middle line:84%
And they are still
today in Palestine.

00:48:12.220 --> 00:48:14.590 align:middle line:90%
They survived.

00:48:14.590 --> 00:48:17.710 align:middle line:84%
Time came and I had
to go to the army.

00:48:17.710 --> 00:48:19.690 align:middle line:90%
I had to leave.

00:48:19.690 --> 00:48:22.700 align:middle line:84%
And here is the saddest
moment of my life.

00:48:22.700 --> 00:48:26.340 align:middle line:84%
I kissed my parents
and my sisters goodbye.

00:48:26.340 --> 00:48:27.760 align:middle line:90%
I said, I'll be back soon.

00:48:27.760 --> 00:48:28.960 align:middle line:90%
And I'll be watching you.

00:48:28.960 --> 00:48:32.110 align:middle line:84%
And that's the
last time I ever--

00:48:32.110 --> 00:48:32.740 align:middle line:90%
Saw them.

00:48:32.740 --> 00:48:33.385 align:middle line:90%
--see them.

00:48:33.385 --> 00:48:35.015 align:middle line:90%
So you went into the army then?

00:48:35.015 --> 00:48:35.890 align:middle line:90%
I went into the army.

00:48:35.890 --> 00:48:36.820 align:middle line:90%
Where did you go?

00:48:36.820 --> 00:48:40.270 align:middle line:90%
I went called a city Nagybánya.

00:48:40.270 --> 00:48:41.860 align:middle line:90%
How far was that from home?

00:48:41.860 --> 00:48:48.310 align:middle line:84%
From home, that was, oh,
about four or five hours' ride

00:48:48.310 --> 00:48:49.480 align:middle line:90%
on a train.

00:48:49.480 --> 00:48:52.810 align:middle line:84%
And there-- now,
I'm leaving home.

00:48:52.810 --> 00:48:55.510 align:middle line:84%
I don't know anything
what's going on home.

00:48:55.510 --> 00:48:56.692 align:middle line:90%
I'm different.

00:48:56.692 --> 00:48:57.400 align:middle line:90%
No communication.

00:48:57.400 --> 00:48:58.825 align:middle line:90%
No communications whatsoever.

00:48:58.825 --> 00:48:59.830 align:middle line:90%
No letters, nothing.

00:48:59.830 --> 00:49:00.970 align:middle line:90%
I left home.

00:49:00.970 --> 00:49:05.140 align:middle line:84%
And I don't know anything
till after the war,

00:49:05.140 --> 00:49:07.658 align:middle line:84%
I'm finding out
details from my sister.

00:49:07.658 --> 00:49:08.200 align:middle line:90%
I understand.

00:49:08.200 --> 00:49:09.367 align:middle line:90%
But till then, I don't know.

00:49:09.367 --> 00:49:12.610 align:middle line:84%
But let's talk about--
you went to the army.

00:49:12.610 --> 00:49:16.840 align:middle line:84%
Now, how long did
you stay in the army?

00:49:16.840 --> 00:49:19.450 align:middle line:84%
Here is a different--
when you say army,

00:49:19.450 --> 00:49:20.560 align:middle line:90%
it's a different concept.

00:49:20.560 --> 00:49:25.110 align:middle line:84%
You got to understand,
here, with the army,

00:49:25.110 --> 00:49:32.500 align:middle line:84%
I happened to have that
we had a colonel who

00:49:32.500 --> 00:49:39.280 align:middle line:84%
was a very good guy, who later
became one of those Righteous--

00:49:39.280 --> 00:49:39.880 align:middle line:90%
Gentiles.

00:49:39.880 --> 00:49:41.230 align:middle line:90%
--Gentiles.

00:49:41.230 --> 00:49:44.320 align:middle line:84%
His son is writing a book
right now in Budapest.

00:49:44.320 --> 00:49:46.460 align:middle line:90%
And my name will play a part.

00:49:46.460 --> 00:49:51.070 align:middle line:84%
What is this man's
name, the colonel?

00:49:51.070 --> 00:49:52.090 align:middle line:90%
Gee.

00:49:52.090 --> 00:49:54.130 align:middle line:84%
Or his son's name,
do you recall?

00:49:54.130 --> 00:49:56.690 align:middle line:90%
He was called Colonel Kelety.

00:49:56.690 --> 00:49:57.510 align:middle line:90%
Kelety.

00:49:57.510 --> 00:49:58.230 align:middle line:90%
Kelety.

00:49:58.230 --> 00:49:58.810 align:middle line:90%
Calady.

00:49:58.810 --> 00:49:59.530 align:middle line:90%
Kelety, yeah.

00:49:59.530 --> 00:50:00.580 align:middle line:90%
Can you spell it?

00:50:00.580 --> 00:50:02.520 align:middle line:90%
K-E-L-E-T-Y.

00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:03.160 align:middle line:90%
Oh, OK.

00:50:03.160 --> 00:50:04.750 align:middle line:90%
And he's going display.

00:50:04.750 --> 00:50:09.650 align:middle line:84%
He's playing a-- he's writing--
his son is putting together

00:50:09.650 --> 00:50:10.150 align:middle line:90%
a book.

00:50:10.150 --> 00:50:12.250 align:middle line:84%
He was here in America
not too long ago.

00:50:12.250 --> 00:50:14.080 align:middle line:90%
And he was there and back.

00:50:14.080 --> 00:50:16.840 align:middle line:84%
And I have a special
story with him.

00:50:16.840 --> 00:50:20.320 align:middle line:84%
And he dedicated quite
a little bit to that.

00:50:20.320 --> 00:50:21.300 align:middle line:90%
How wonderful.

00:50:21.300 --> 00:50:22.270 align:middle line:90%
Now, tell me.

00:50:22.270 --> 00:50:24.670 align:middle line:84%
So Colonel Kelety was
helpful to the Jewish

00:50:24.670 --> 00:50:25.360 align:middle line:90%
To Jewish-- he--

00:50:25.360 --> 00:50:26.050 align:middle line:90%
--the Jewish people in the army.

00:50:26.050 --> 00:50:28.360 align:middle line:84%
--he was the one who
issued those papers.

00:50:28.360 --> 00:50:32.140 align:middle line:84%
But he didn't know that in
between, the between-goers

00:50:32.140 --> 00:50:33.650 align:middle line:90%
made money out of that.

00:50:33.650 --> 00:50:34.150 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:50:34.150 --> 00:50:34.650 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:50:34.650 --> 00:50:36.025 align:middle line:84%
So in other words,
he was the one

00:50:36.025 --> 00:50:37.220 align:middle line:90%
who put the signature on it.

00:50:37.220 --> 00:50:38.470 align:middle line:90%
And he is the one who was in--

00:50:38.470 --> 00:50:39.795 align:middle line:90%
To call you to the army.

00:50:39.795 --> 00:50:43.775 align:middle line:84%
To come in to be under his
regiment, in other words,

00:50:43.775 --> 00:50:44.275 align:middle line:90%
under his.

00:50:44.275 --> 00:50:46.090 align:middle line:90%
Sure, I understand.

00:50:46.090 --> 00:50:47.740 align:middle line:90%
So we came in there.

00:50:47.740 --> 00:50:48.460 align:middle line:90%
I reported.

00:50:48.460 --> 00:50:51.520 align:middle line:84%
I was taken in,
registered, everything,

00:50:51.520 --> 00:50:54.850 align:middle line:90%
issued certain military things--

00:50:54.850 --> 00:50:57.430 align:middle line:84%
a blanket and other
few little things.

00:50:57.430 --> 00:50:58.450 align:middle line:90%
Uniform, yeah.

00:50:58.450 --> 00:51:00.380 align:middle line:90%
No uniform, just on our own--

00:51:00.380 --> 00:51:01.615 align:middle line:90%
we went in our own clothes.

00:51:01.615 --> 00:51:02.020 align:middle line:90%
Your own clothing, OK.

00:51:02.020 --> 00:51:02.520 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:51:02.520 --> 00:51:06.790 align:middle line:84%
And we just received-- there
was a armband with a stamp in it

00:51:06.790 --> 00:51:08.440 align:middle line:90%
from the Hungarian Army.

00:51:08.440 --> 00:51:11.440 align:middle line:84%
and this yellow band,
yellow armband, and this

00:51:11.440 --> 00:51:12.437 align:middle line:90%
is what we wore.

00:51:12.437 --> 00:51:14.270 align:middle line:84%
This tells that you're
a member of the army.

00:51:14.270 --> 00:51:15.200 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:51:15.200 --> 00:51:18.410 align:middle line:84%
Now, as long as
I'm in the armband,

00:51:18.410 --> 00:51:20.540 align:middle line:90%
let me go back to the four--

00:51:20.540 --> 00:51:22.040 align:middle line:90%
I didn't talk about it.

00:51:22.040 --> 00:51:24.830 align:middle line:84%
It was in the ghetto, when
we came in the ghetto,

00:51:24.830 --> 00:51:27.890 align:middle line:84%
that everybody had to
wear the yellow star.

00:51:27.890 --> 00:51:32.240 align:middle line:90%
And we had to-- should stop?

00:51:32.240 --> 00:51:32.930 align:middle line:90%
No, go ahead.

00:51:32.930 --> 00:51:34.820 align:middle line:90%
We had the yellow star.

00:51:34.820 --> 00:51:40.130 align:middle line:84%
We had to wear the yellow star,
and of course, a strict curfew.

00:51:40.130 --> 00:51:42.010 align:middle line:90%
You couldn't go out from--

00:51:42.010 --> 00:51:43.010 align:middle line:90%
Sure, the curfew, right.

00:51:43.010 --> 00:51:47.610 align:middle line:84%
Right, and all the
restrictions that go with it.

00:51:47.610 --> 00:51:50.660 align:middle line:90%
Now, back to the army.

00:51:50.660 --> 00:51:55.610 align:middle line:84%
I was been in there for
about four or five days.

00:51:55.610 --> 00:51:59.900 align:middle line:84%
We received word that
the local Jewish people

00:51:59.900 --> 00:52:02.840 align:middle line:90%
have been taken to the ghettos.

00:52:02.840 --> 00:52:05.210 align:middle line:84%
In other words, they
created the same ghetto

00:52:05.210 --> 00:52:09.800 align:middle line:84%
that we had in our town
hometown, we created here.

00:52:09.800 --> 00:52:13.650 align:middle line:84%
In order to know what's
going on, we right away--

00:52:13.650 --> 00:52:15.440 align:middle line:90%
some of the guys there knew me.

00:52:15.440 --> 00:52:18.590 align:middle line:84%
And we felt that something
is going to happen,

00:52:18.590 --> 00:52:21.860 align:middle line:84%
some different organization
because of the Zionist movement

00:52:21.860 --> 00:52:23.030 align:middle line:90%
that I used to be.

00:52:23.030 --> 00:52:24.920 align:middle line:90%
I used to organize and all that.

00:52:24.920 --> 00:52:27.980 align:middle line:84%
Right away, I organized a
small group of guys who had--

00:52:27.980 --> 00:52:29.950 align:middle line:90%
a hard core of guys around me.

00:52:29.950 --> 00:52:30.590 align:middle line:90%
Had what?

00:52:30.590 --> 00:52:32.526 align:middle line:90%
A hard core of guys.

00:52:32.526 --> 00:52:33.026 align:middle line:90%
Hard core.

00:52:33.026 --> 00:52:34.610 align:middle line:90%
Oh, to do what?

00:52:34.610 --> 00:52:35.640 align:middle line:90%
As we will keep going.

00:52:35.640 --> 00:52:36.140 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:52:36.140 --> 00:52:36.932 align:middle line:90%
Well, but we have--

00:52:36.932 --> 00:52:39.520 align:middle line:84%
Whatever is going needed,
whatever will be needed to do.

00:52:39.520 --> 00:52:40.020 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:52:40.020 --> 00:52:40.980 align:middle line:90%
But you're in the army.

00:52:40.980 --> 00:52:41.480 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:52:41.480 --> 00:52:41.690 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:52:41.690 --> 00:52:42.470 align:middle line:90%
And we are in the army.

00:52:42.470 --> 00:52:42.970 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:52:42.970 --> 00:52:44.630 align:middle line:90%
Let's take a little break now.

00:52:44.630 --> 00:52:48.080 align:middle line:84%
And we'll come back and
finish this interesting story.

00:52:48.080 --> 00:52:48.640 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:52:48.640 --> 00:52:49.140 align:middle line:90%
All right?

00:52:49.140 --> 00:52:50.920 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:52:50.920 --> 00:53:09.000 align:middle line:90%